commit 902ec19a3aed66674629ce7c2dd570e0be59e6a9
Author: sebastianbuzdugan <81054605+sebastianbuzdugan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 21 08:17:40 2026 +0300

    Fix gate --ci flag passthrough, eval toxicity references leak, and failing tests
    
    - frai gate init --ci silently dropped --ci: the root command's own --ci
      flag consumed it before it reached the gate subcommand. Enable
      positional options and pass through options on the gate command.
    - Default toxicity metric received the references array as its
      banned-terms list, flagging any output that contained its reference.
      Wrap it in DEFAULT_METRICS so only outputs are passed.
    - Export finetune schema constants from finetune/index.js as named
      exports (governance test imports APPROVAL_STATUSES).
    - Align governance summary test with the blocked-status vocabulary.
    - Run vitest in run mode for frai and frai-core test scripts.
    - Exclude test files from the frai-core npm package.
    - Bump frai to 1.1.5 and frai-core to 0.0.2; depend on published
      versions instead of workspace:* so npm installs work.

